# earlyoom settings for notifier's host (notifier#74).
#
# Install to /etc/default/earlyoom; see docs/RUNBOOK.md.
#
# Why an early killer at all. The kernel's own OOM killer is the last resort,
# and on a host with no swap it is late: there is no slow path into pressure,
# so by the time it acts the atomic-allocation failures in unrelated processes
# have already landed — which is the whole failure mode, since on broker
# nothing was OOM-killed at all (references/troubleshooting.md row U).
# earlyoom watches MemAvailable and acts while the host still responds.
#
# -m 12,6: SIGTERM at 12% available (~470 MiB), SIGKILL at 6% (~235 MiB).
# Above the 10,5 default because with no swap the reclaim that would normally
# buy time does not exist, so the warning shot has to come earlier.
#
# --avoid is belt and braces over the OOMScoreAdjust=-500 the production units
# now carry, which earlyoom already honours: `uv` is status.service's own
# MainPID comm (uvicorn runs beneath it), and the API is useless without
# postgres or the tailnet it binds to.
#
# --prefer names the measured cause rather than the victim: the agent sessions
# (`claude`, and `MainThread` — node renames its main thread) and the servers
# they launch. `npm exec socrat` is the SocratiCode server; comm is truncated
# to 15 characters, hence the start-anchored `^npm` rather than a full match.
# Losing a session costs a session. Losing the service costs the bus.
#
# NO SPACES inside either regex. earlyoom.service is
# `ExecStart=/usr/bin/earlyoom $EARLYOOM_ARGS`, unquoted, so systemd splits on
# whitespace with no shell quoting — a space would silently become a second
# argument, earlyoom would exit on it, and the host would be left with no
# early killer. tests/deploy/test_memory_reservation.py asserts this.
EARLYOOM_ARGS="-r 3600 -m 12,6 --avoid ^(uv|uvicorn|postgres|tailscaled|systemd|sshd|exe-init)$ --prefer ^(MainThread|claude|npm|node|npx)"
